        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I have another question but I don't want to open a new issue, how can I substitute ' for \" if I'm at the beginning of the line? Example: helloworld(' some word '), I still haven't been able to do it, which with vim-surround was just cs'\"\r\n\r\nIf it is like `^helloworld(' some word ')` then 'mini.surround' won't work (`^` - cursor). It works only for surroundings that cover cursor (when cursor is between left and right surrounding).\r\n\r\nIf it is like `helloworld('^ some word ')`, try `sr'\"` ('surround' 'replace').",
